<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Frisii</h1><p class="st-meta">100 BCE – 400 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Germanic people of the North Sea coast who lived on artificial mounds and defied Rome by force and by diplomacy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Frisii lived on the coastal marshes of the northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and the Ems. To survive floods they built terps, artificial dwelling mounds raised over generations. They became tributaries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> after the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero-claudius-drusus">Drusus</a> in 12 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They paid tribute in ox hides. Roman sources describe no kings but war leaders and envoys; in 58 CE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verritus">Verritus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malorix">Malorix</a> travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and boldly took seats among the senators at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a>, winning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero's</a> admiration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 28 CE they revolted against exactions, hanging tax collectors and defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-baduhenna-wood">Baduhenna wood</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> later abandoned control. In the 4th century rising seas left much of the coast nearly deserted, and the area was resettled, later forming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/frisian-kingdom">Frisian Kingdom</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/frisii.jpg" alt="Frisii" width="320" height="345"><figcaption>Image: my work · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Continental.coast.150AD.Germanic.peoples.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 BCE – 400 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Verritus, Malorix</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Germanic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Proto-Germanic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Frisians</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=frisii" aria-label="Frisii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4807 361 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Frisii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5127 617h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5127 617h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Netherlands. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=frisii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

